<article class="env-remark" id="0ER3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ER3">Remark <span data-tag="0ER3">82.22.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X' \to X$ be a morphism of good algebraic spaces over $B$ as in Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a>. Let $(\mathcal{L}, s, i : D \to X)$ be a triple as in Definition <a href="/tag/0ER1" data-tag="0ER1">82.22.1</a>. Then we can set $\mathcal{L}' = f^*\mathcal{L}$, $s' = f^*s$, and $D' = X' \times _ X D = Z(s')$. This gives a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ D' \ar[d]_ g \ar[r]_{i'} &  X' \ar[d]^ f \\  D \ar[r]^ i &  X }  \]
</div>
  <p> and we can ask for various compatibilities between $i^*$ and $(i')^*$. </p>
</article>